KiCad libraries
===============

Kairo reads the symbol, footprint and 3D-model libraries of the user's own
KiCad install and copies none of them into this repository. A schematic or
board Kairo writes, like one drawn in KiCad, embeds the symbols and
footprints it uses. The KiCad libraries are licensed CC-BY-SA-4.0 with an
exception that waives the licence's terms for designs made with them and
the files generated from them (https://www.kicad.org/libraries/license/);
the schematics under evals/ that Kairo generated are such files.


Test data
=========

tests/fixtures/kicad10/netlist/mikoto.net is the netlist kicad-cli 10.0.6
wrote for the mikoto board listed below.

tests/fixtures/kicad10/erc/*.json are ERC reports that kicad-cli 10.0.6
wrote for copies of demo projects shipped with KiCad (share/kicad/demos).
They are KiCad's output, kept so the ERC classifier is tested against what
KiCad really writes; no demo project file is copied into this repository.
The KiCad-backed tests copy the installed demos into a temporary folder at
run time. See tests/fixtures/kicad10/erc/README.md.

tests/fixtures/real/ holds sixteen open-hardware KiCad projects, unmodified,
each under its own licence with the licence text beside it. See
tests/fixtures/real/README.md for what was left out of each. ERC reports
and a netlist that kicad-cli wrote for some of them are under
tests/fixtures/kicad10/.

